<!-- The CAAF brief's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of the typst
     template (Times New Roman) at 14 pt (size 28 half points; Rule 37(a): 14-point type, footnotes included); Body
     Text in 25.9 pt line boxes (typst pitch-double) with a half-inch first-line indent; quotations and footnotes in
     14.4 pt boxes (typst pitch-single), 14 pt around a quotation, 7 pt after a footnote; the footer 35.9 pt from the
     page edge. armfor.lua sets every other paragraph's own spacing. Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="28" body="518" single="288" indent="720" quote="280" note-after="140" footer="718"/>
